      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 4,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "diagram",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "clean",
          "accent": "blue",
          "decor": false
        },
        "presenterNotes": "Dispatch. The orchestrator (the captain, in the factory's terms) consults the queue of related tickets and writes back to it. fleetd has already done the deterministic part — dependencies, blockers — so the orchestrator only makes the judgment call: is this ticket Ready? Yes → a worktree is cut and the ticket is dispatched. No → hold; once fixed it's re-queued."
      },
      "name": "Dispatch"
    },
