    {
      "id": "KiN-ElU6B18OJo5HfMWnW",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 18240,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1080,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1203331030,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1586252321,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795209339684,
      "created": 1795209339684,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 8,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "diagram",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "clean",
          "accent": "blue",
          "decor": false
        },
        "presenterNotes": "The sightline — the whole system in one opaque view, rendered live by the same React-Flow renderer as the demos/fleet/viewer viewer (vendored, read-only), so it always matches the code. Operator → wraps judgment in /fleet-* skills → fleetc (the CLI) → fleetd (the daemon) → which actuates the tracker and forge, spawns the crew, works the project worktrees, and persists everything to the ledger, which the dashboard reads. Pan/zoom to walk it."
      },
      "name": "Architecture"
    },
    {
      "id": "vCUzY9RfqspZSBfMe2llN",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 20510,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1080,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1647872790,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1673124170,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795209339773,
      "created": 1795209339773,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 9,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "diagram",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "clean",
          "accent": "blue",
          "decor": false
        },
        "presenterNotes": "The engine — fleetd's heart is one loop on one thread (scheduler.rs::run). It isn't a pipeline: each pass just runs whatever is due, then waits up to half a second for a command. Observe, every ~5s: which agent sessions are alive — read-only, nothing written. Sync, every ~5 minutes: copy Jira tickets and GitLab MRs into the ledger, our database. Actuate: this is where the world changes — immediately when a fleetc command arrives (from me or from an agent), and every ~60s when reconcile compares intent with reality and spawns, hands off, reaps or heals. All writes go through this one thread, so there's never a race. Stop fleetd and the loop ends — the factory is off."
      },
      "name": "The Engine"
    },
